	"_comment": "The Girdle (W19): a wall of crag, boulder and standing stone 56 m across, broken on one bearing. It is ONE layout rather than a ring of rock sites because the suite makes every pair of sites keep 1.5 m of daylight between their real footprints, and a crag's footprint is 13 m wide -- so a ring tight enough to read as a wall is a ring of sites that overlap. Pieces inside a layout may touch, which is what a rock wall does. The gap faces south-east, toward the rest of the Vale, with a fire either side of it.",
